{"id":"u-0521b083-ad72-4f63-91f5-7b9c300e13ea","src":"community","title":"Science Based PPLUL + Core","author":"Paul  B.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/6N7gtj-science-based-pplul","desc":"Science proved PPLUP with core engagement exercises \n\n📈\nProgressive Overload\nAdd weight or reps each week. Track every session. If you can hit the top of the rep range, add 2.5–5 lbs next session.\n\n🎯\nProximity to Failure\nEnd sets at RIR 1–3 (1–3 reps in reserve). Going to absolute failure too often increases injury risk without added benefit.\n\n🔄\nRep Range Variety\nMix 5–8 (strength), 8–15 (moderate), and 15–30 (pump/endurance) ranges. All build muscle, but variety is protective and comprehensive.\n\n⏱️\nRest Periods\n2–3 min for compounds, 60–90 sec for isolations. Cutting rest too short reduces output and total volume — don't rush.\n\n\n🥩\nNutrition\nAim for 0.7–1g protein/lb bodyweight. Caloric surplus of 200–500 kcal/day for lean bulking. Sleep 7–9 hours.\n\n🔁\nDeload Every 6–8 Weeks\nReduce volume or intensity by ~50% for one week. This is when supercompensation occurs and strength/size gains solidify.\n\n\n\n.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":10,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-01T05:07:54.562Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["PUSH","PULL","LEGS","UPPER","LOWER"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Cable Fly (Low To High)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Overhead Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pallof Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[